    "title": "Count Good Nodes in a Binary Tree",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given a binary tree, a node is considered good if no ancestor on the path from the root has a value greater than the node's value. Determine the total number of good nodes.",
